cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  qSHA256: reversible quantum circuit construction, verification and
  resource analysis for SHA-2 and SHA-3
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: icedmoca
    email: blazehavenservers@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/icedmoca/qSHA256
license: Apache-2.0
version: 2.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-17
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - reversible computing
  - resource estimation
  - SHA-256
  - SHA-3
  - Grover
  - Clifford+T
  - fault tolerance
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  qSHA256 builds SHA-2 and SHA-3 out of reversible quantum circuits, proves
  them correct with a SAT-based equivalence checker, measures their logical
  resource requirements, and searches a design space for cheaper
  implementations. Correctness is established by symbolic execution into an
  XOR-aware And-Inverter Graph followed by SAT: functional equivalence against
  an independently written specification, ancilla cleanliness, and Gidney AND
  preconditions are each proved over all inputs rather than sampled. The
  message schedule's register count is shown optimal via the reversible pebble
  game, and Ch, Maj and the Gidney adder are shown optimal in AND count against
  proven multiplicative-complexity lower bounds. Reported figures distinguish
  measured, transpiled, analytical, extrapolated and assumption-dependent
  quantities throughout.
